<div class="absolute top-0 let-0 w-full h-full overflow-y-scroll scroll-smooth no-scrollbar" web:root="override">
    <helm-nav></helm-nav>
    <main id="main">
        <!--- Hero --->
        <div class="relative w-full flex flex-col items-center">
            <!--- Lines --->
            <helm-container class="absolute border-x border-edge mx-16 h-full">
            </helm-container>
            <!--- Wave --->
            <div class="absolute inset-[-76px_0px_0px_48px]">
                <div data-js-target="nouveau-bloom-wave" class="relative w-full h-full"></div>
            </div>
            <!--- Hero --->
            <helm-section class="relative">
                <helm-container class="relative h-dvh flex flex-col justify-center px-16 pb-144">
                    <h1 class="text-48/100 tracking-tighter max-w-656 mb-24">
                        Implement consistent core tokens, <span class="text-neutral-400">ship new work, org-wide, faster</span>
                    </h1>
                    <p class="text-18/[137.5%] text-content max-w-576">
                        Helm and Sail are already almost the same. Why not make them one? <span class="whitespace-nowrap">Or, at</span> least, make them share the same foundations? In this prototype, <span class="whitespace-nowrap">I loosely</span> explore what it would take to get us there.
                    </p>
                </helm-container>
            </helm-section>
        </div>
    </main>
    <helm-footer></helm-footer>
</div>